# spark in w3m -- your own AI, on your own machine (spark.forgewright.ai).
# Append this to your own ~/.w3m/keymap (and cgi_bin to ~/.w3m/config;
# the README's three install lines do both):
#
#     cat ~/.w3m/spark/keymap.spark >> ~/.w3m/keymap
#
# One key, spark's key in every app: M-s (Esc then s). The page you
# are reading is stashed and the spark page opens -- a page like any
# other, drawn by w3m itself:
#
#   spark> [field]     your question: type, Enter, ask ("does it
#                      mention prices"; a leading ? works too)
#   overview           a link: what does this page cover?
#   part 1 . part 2    links, on a page past 16 kB: read one part
#   B                  never mind -- back to the page you were reading
#
# The answer is a page too, every line quoting the source, the field
# repeated below it for the follow-up; when the page does not answer,
# the reply is one line showing its own opening words -- never a
# guess. Nothing leaves this machine but the rendered page text and
# your words, to the brain spark is configured for -- no URL, no
# path. Needs w3m 0.5.3 or newer and spark 1.20 or newer. M-s is a
# suggestion (w3m's own M-s, save buffer, moves aside) -- edit the
# line to taste.
keymap M-s COMMAND "PIPE_BUF 'spark-w3m --stash'; GOTO file:///cgi-bin/spark.cgi"
